{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLCredit","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLCreditV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLCredit"}],"title":"MXLCredit"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLCredit","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By default, a series of credit-words and credit-symbol elements within a single credit element follow one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"another in sequence visually. Non-positional formatting attributes are carried over from the previous element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The page attribute for the credit element specifies the page number where the credit should appear. This is an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integer value that starts with 1 for the first page. Its value is 1 by default. Since credits occur before the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"music, these page numbers do not refer to the page numbering specified by the print element’s page-number","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The credit-type element indicates the purpose behind a credit. Multiple types of data may be combined in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"single credit, so multiple elements may be used. Standard values include page number, title, subtitle,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"composer, arranger, lyricist, rights, and part name.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<credit>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The credit type represents the appearance of the title, composer, arranger, lyricist, copyright, dedication,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and other text, symbols, and graphics that commonly appear on the first page of a score. The credit-words,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"credit-symbol, and credit-image elements are similar to the words, symbol, and image elements for directions."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"However, since the credit is not part of a measure, the default-x and default-y attributes adjust the origin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative to the bottom left-hand corner of the page. The enclosure for credit-words and credit-symbol is none"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by default."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcredit"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLCredit\/init(id:kind:link:bookmark:content:page:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc: